{"name":"Ginger Flower","hex":"#cf524e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ginger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pungent aromatic rhizome of a tropical Asian herb, Zingiber officinale, used as a spice and as a stimulant and acarminative.","The plant that produces this rhizome."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown color.","Having hair or fur of this color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ginger"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ginger","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger is a flowering plant whose rhizome, ginger root or ginger, is widely used as a spice and a folk medicine. It is an herbaceous perennial that grows annual pseudostems about one meter tall, bearing narrow leaf blades. The inflorescences bear flowers having pale yellow petals with purple edges, and arise directly from the rhizome on separate shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger","wikidata":"Q35625"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Ginger_inflorescence.jpg/500px-Ginger_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Ginger_inflorescence.jpg/1280px-Ginger_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Ginger_inflorescence.jpg/500px-Ginger_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGinger_inflorescence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg/500px-Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg/1280px-Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg/500px-Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ginger flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlower_of_Ginger1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Gingerfield.jpg/500px-Gingerfield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp